.TH AVR\-GROUP\-USAGE 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-group-usage \- Show the vCPU a group uses and the limits on its path.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr group usage
[OPTIONS] GROUP
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the vCPU a group uses and the limits on its path.
.PP
GROUP is a group ID (grp-...), the group's path from the root group, such as Organization/Platform/CI, or the end of a path when only one group has it, such as Platform/CI.
.PP
Usage counts the group and its subgroups.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr group usage Platform
    avr group usage Platform --json used_vcpu,pools
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    group_id, group_state, measured_at, pools, used_vcpu
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIGROUP\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-group (1),
.BR avr-group-create (1),
.BR avr-group-delete (1),
.BR avr-group-edit (1),
.BR avr-group-limit (1),
.BR avr-group-list (1),
.BR avr-group-member (1),
.BR avr-group-view (1)
